From: rcllf <noreply@rcllf.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rcllf marker for 0007-federate-dnet-handler-env-mutex

Puts the string "rcllf-reactor-c-patch:0007-federate-dnet-handler-env-mutex"
into section rcllf_reactor_c_patches of every program that compiles this file.
A tool can read the section back from the running program to check that
a configured patch is present.

The hunk removes and re-adds a line that only the fix has, so it applies only on
top of the fix. The marker sits outside the fix hunks' context, so the fix patch
still reads "previously applied" on a tree that has both. federate.c is compiled
into federated programs only.

Rcllf-Marker-For: 0007-federate-dnet-handler-env-mutex
Rcllf-Marker-Scope: federated
---
--- a/core/federated/federate.c
+++ b/core/federated/federate.c
@@ -1472,10 +1472,17 @@
  * the main thread had already replaced by a newer one (or by NEVER), the RTI
  * recorded the federate's next event in its past, and the federation stalled
- * (brake_fusion fed1host under CPU stress).
+ * (brake_fusion fed1host under CPU stress).
  */
 static void handle_downstream_next_event_tag() {
   size_t bytes_to_read = sizeof(instant_t) + sizeof(microstep_t);
   unsigned char buffer[bytes_to_read];
+  {
+    // rcllf patch marker: the benchmark harness reads it back from the running
+    // program. The hunk also rewrites a line of the fix, so it applies only on top of it.
+    static const char rcllf_marker[]
+        __attribute__((section("rcllf_reactor_c_patches"), used, unused)) =
+        "rcllf-reactor-c-patch:0007-federate-dnet-handler-env-mutex";
+  }
   read_from_net_fail_on_error(_fed.net_to_RTI, bytes_to_read, buffer,
                               "Failed to read downstream next event tag from RTI.");
   tag_t DNET = extract_tag(buffer);
